      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    long long n;\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n\n    printf(\"%lld\", n);\n    while (n >= 10) {\n        long long sum = 0, x = n;\n        while (x > 0) {\n            sum += x % 10;\n            x /= 10;\n        }\n        n = sum;\n        printf(\" %lld\", n);\n    }\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}",
      "statement": "Given a positive integer [[n]], repeatedly replace it by the sum of its decimal digits until a single digit remains.\nPrint the whole chain of values, from [[n]] to the final single digit, with the values separated by single spaces.",
